From: accord-eps-torque-mod analysis, 2026-09-20
Subject: [PATCH] Accord: allow margin-safe loop gain -- raise the SteerKP ceiling and
 schedule the error-notch Q by speed

Apply on StarPilot branch `Dom`, which was clean at 84766cdc5 when this was written:

    cd C:/Users/dudei/Desktop/Projects/openpilots/raayyymond-StarPilot/StarPilot
    git checkout Dom && git status --porcelain     # expect empty
    git apply --check analysis-2020accord/reference/starpilot_Dom_margin-safe-gain.patch
    git apply           <same path>

WHY, IN ONE PARAGRAPH.  On the operator's own goal metric -- how closely achieved lateral acceleration tracks
the model's desired lateral acceleration, with V282 as the reference -- the torque-mode build sits at J 1.3512
against V282's 0.442, and 98% of that gap is in 0.15-0.60 Hz.  It is a LOOP GAIN deficit: the fork's lateral
loop never crosses unity (|L| < 1 at every frequency 0.08-2.5 Hz) where V282's crossed at 0.26-0.37 Hz on its
proportional term alone.  Raising SteerKP closes it, but the gain also lands at 3.4-4.9 Hz, where the V293 plant
is 5-13x more compliant than V282's rate-servo EPS was, and that is where the stability margin binds.  The fix
is not more gain and not less -- it is gain PAIRED WITH a wider error notch, which holds 3.4-4.9 Hz down while
0.15-0.60 Hz goes up.  Today the toggle ceilings forbid that pairing: SteerKP stops at 3.00, and a Q wide enough
to protect at speed is unsafe below 15 m/s because the notch centre falls to 0.82-1.28 Hz there.  This patch
removes exactly those two obstacles and nothing else.

MEASURED, at matched vector margin (VM = min|1+L| over 2-6 Hz; anchors below):
    toggles only     SteerKP 3.0 / Q 0.30  ->  15.9% of the gap, command shake x0.964, VM 0.479/0.377
    with this patch  SteerKP 5.0 / Q 0.20  ->  23.1% of the gap, command shake x0.973, VM 0.396/0.388
    with this patch  SteerKP 6.0 / Q 0.20  ->  32.9% of the gap, command shake x1.004, VM 0.281/0.290
VM anchors, each computed from that route's own identified plant and its own flown controller:
    V282 0.842/0.882 | r73 0.913/0.828 | r72 (flew clean) -/0.527 | rev 6.4 as flown 0.686/0.505
    r71 (LIMIT-CYCLED at 2.34 Hz) 0.322/0.079

DEFAULTS ARE BIT-IDENTICAL TO TODAY.  Hunk 1 changes only a clamp ceiling, so every existing value is unaffected.
Hunk 2's schedule interpolates [8, 15] m/s from max(q, 1.0) to q, so at the shipped default q = 1.0 it returns
1.0 at every speed -- exactly today's behaviour -- and at any q < 1.0 it leaves everything below 8 m/s at the
1.0 that has already driven.  q <= 0 (notch bypassed) passes straight through, preserving that escape.

NOT IN THIS PATCH, DELIBERATELY:
 - a k_d / derivative term.  Measured VM 0.048 at KP 4.0 / Q 0.30 / k_d 0.40 -- identical to the withdrawn
   ARM-KP2, i.e. the worst on the ladder.  k_d is measurement-rate feedback through a 2 Hz low-pass, so it adds
   gain exactly where the margin binds.
 - decoupling the integrator from kp in error_with_lsf (torque.py:342).  The defect is real -- kp sits in the
   integrator's denominator, so SteerKP 1->3 cuts low-speed integral authority to x0.35 at 2 m/s -- but the
   existing AccordTorqueKi toggle reaches x3.33 and covers SteerKP 3-4 with room.  Ship the toggle, measure,
   and only write code if SteerKP > 4 is ever wanted.
 - any firmware change.  Nothing here touches the EPS.

